      "writtenOn": "2023-04-26T17:00:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This split seems a bit arbitrary, since there are still a lot of fan settings in `thermal.c`, like all of the `FAN_` macros. How will it be decided which fan-related functions/macros/definitions go here versus `thermal.c`?",
      "revId": "529fb159048a02b754c31ef015f0c40dac264779",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b255012f_bb7f35c3",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/skyrim/winterhold/src/fan.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1565377
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-27T09:59:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d argue that this belongs to fan.c because the logic here has nothing to do with thermals/sensors.\nThe input here is the current/target RPM and the result is a call to the PWM that changes fan duty.\nOn the other hand frostflow logic in \"thermal.c\" does something slightly different; It selects the target RPM based on temperature read from a sensor.\nIn my opinion this is how the distinction should be made.\nIt matches what is done in `zephyr/shim/src/fan.c`",
      "parentUuid": "c0670ecf_84c3e2b5",
      "revId": "529fb159048a02b754c31ef015f0c40dac264779",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "73d5bf14_2c0f9094",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/skyrim/winterhold/src/fan.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-27T14:54:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`thermal.c` sets the policy to map temperature ranges to fan actions, while this file manages the setting the fan speed.\n\nEventually this file will be eliminated once a shared PID algorithm gets implemented.  All the `struct ec_thermal_config` arrays in `thermal.c` will  still be used with the fan control.",
      "parentUuid": "c0670ecf_84c3e2b5",
      "revId": "529fb159048a02b754c31ef015f0c40dac264779",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "264f8a0b_05a082ca",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/skyrim/winterhold/src/fan.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1565377
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-27T15:27:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "```\nEventually this file will be eliminated once a shared PID algorithm gets implemented. All the struct ec_thermal_config arrays in thermal.c will still be used with the fan control.\n```\n\nI don\u0027t think that\u0027s the case. The PID controls fan duty based on current and target RPM. My intention is to use it as an alternative to `fan_smart_control`.\nThe logic that sets target RPM based on sensor readings is a separate thing.",
      "parentUuid": "73d5bf14_2c0f9094",
      "revId": "529fb159048a02b754c31ef015f0c40dac264779",
